<http://data.silknow.org/object/9ea83aff-ff91-3024-bdbd-09eb7ad310e5>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Bed cover of block-printed cotton. With stems of an exotic flower reserved in white, with a horseshoe-shaped half calyx in red and pink, and long leaves in pencilled blue, all set in a deep madder ground of purple-maroon. Made up from narrow strips, the widest being approximately 21 inches, on a very coarse backing of unbleached linen. The scalloped hanging side of the cover are backed with a finer white linen. Scalloped and the join of the top and sides are bound with yellow silk ribbon."@en , "Bed cover of block-printed cotton, made in Europe, 1730-1769"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d95d3157-779f-3678-9677-20f8d5a85407> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Bed cover of block-printed cotton, made in Europe, 1730-1769"@en , "Bed cover of block-printed cotton. With stems of an exotic flower reserved in white, with a horseshoe-shaped half calyx in red and pink, and long leaves in pencilled blue, all set in a deep madder ground of purple-maroon. Made up from narrow strips, the widest being approximately 21 inches, on a very coarse backing of unbleached linen. The scalloped hanging side of the cover are backed with a finer white linen. Scalloped and the join of the top and sides are bound with yellow silk ribbon."@en ;
